{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/912156-suggestions-for-themes-for-a-crossover-game","id":912156,"title":"Suggestions for themes for a crossover game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-11T01:55:20-07:00","id":912156,"title":"Suggestions for themes for a crossover game","content":"I'm musing over the possibility of trying to set up a crossover game involving Beasts, Mages, Vampires and Werewolves (2nd edition). What I'm looking for right now is is advice on potential themes for a campaign, plot hooks,etc, mostly to get my creative juices flowing. I plan on establishing an overarching plot, along with lots of smaller elements for different splats to tie into, so am looking for any ideas folks might have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:18:11-07:00","id":912166,"title":"","content":"The only successful crossover games I've ever run, or played in, weren't about splats.<br /> <br /> They were about people.<br /> <br /> When people have, or form, connections to each other that are strong enough, they're going to find a way to stick together, regardless of the expectations of their respective social hierarchies. If you make the campaign about the characters, instead of about the Invictus Mekhet, the Anakim that hungers for Power, and the Seer who wants out, it's a lot easier to hold everything together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:25:42-07:00","id":912210,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for an overarching theme, you might want to go with Addiction/Need. Mages are Obsessed with Mysteries, the Wolf must Hunt, the Vampire needs Blood, and the Beast Hungers. All four have some sort of compulsion that they need to stay mentally and physically healthy. Thematically, you could exploit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:31:14-07:00","id":912409,"title":"","content":"There is already <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/814497-crossover-help-themes\"><b>a thread about this</b></a>, with some really good posts too.<br /> <br /> It would help if you narrowed down your question. Is there a lot of combat in your games? Or do you prefer investigations and intrigue? How important is the city and its territories in inter-splat conflicts? How much play time is devoted to the more fantastical parts of the setting, like the Astral and the Shadow? Do you prefer the characters to stay closer to the mortal power level in loose terms, or do you like to include allies and antagonists on the epic scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:21:34-07:00","id":912431,"title":"","content":"This is a bit of a silly idea I admit but you could always have it start with old friends meeting up. The grew up together but took very different paths and tries to hide it from their old friends who they think are still mundane. So each one tries to be human thinking the group is all still human untIL it is revealed <br /> <br /> This way the have reasons to trust each other, to care and to be able to work together. It'd also tie into beasts themes as they'd more or less be a disfunction family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T06:06:44-07:00","id":912755,"title":"","content":"Thanks all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm going to bring players in and work with them on making a cohesive cast of characters.<br /> <br /> This is the blurb for the game.<br /> <br /> **<br /> <br /> London is an old city and its roots run deep. Though the city has fallen to plague, fire and war in the past. It endures, it grows and those who call it home remain, no matter how they might be changed by events.<br /> <br /> But cycles of destruction still remain and seem as imprinted on the city as the rest of its heritage, and the new cycle is nowhere near as simple as disease or war.<br /> <br /> A cabal of mages grew curious about seeking out alternative worlds and realities and formed a portal to another Earth with the intention of exploring and learning a whole new reality. None of the four mages who entered ever emerged. But other things did.<br /> <br /> Uratha confined to eternal Gauru form, Mages with unknown Paths, Vampires that could walk in the day, and other, stranger things. These are what try to flee a dying world and unless contained, all of London and beyond is risked.<br /> <br /> **<br /> <br /> My current task is to work on plot hooks and NPCs (friend, foe and both/neither)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:45:40-07:00","id":914111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/912156-suggestions-for-themes-for-a-crossover-game?p=912755#post912755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current task is to work on plot hooks and NPCs (friend, foe and both/neither)</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to check out Climbing the Ladder in VtR 2e core Storytelling chapter and adjust the questions to better fit other supernaturals so that everyone can participate. It takes a bit of time, but it really helps building a core cast for your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T01:39:52-07:00","id":914717,"title":"","content":"Well, if your still looking for opinions I have a few. <br /> <br /> For starters, excellent choice with London as the setting. There is soooooo much supernatural stuff in that city that you really wouldn't need to make up anything new. Just use existing myths with your own twists.<br /> <br /> Second, look for the parallels between gameline but don't be afraid to exclude elements that clash with your Chronicle. If your Chronicle is one focused around exploring mysteries and interacting with the strange then limit your players to Factions dedicated towards exploration and experimentation (like a group consisting of Ordo Dracul, Bone Shadows, and Mysterium characters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T06:27:51-07:00","id":914787,"title":"","content":"Addiction's a good one. Control is another. Figure out what your players are comfortable being present in the game and in background material, and whatever theme you choose, make sure every aspect of your game points to that theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}